                            (Destinations.kt L65; registered in TeslaSyncApplication.kt).

DATA SOURCES (bound through the ViewModel's StateFlow over the KMP core, P1/S8)
  useTrips → TripsRepository.trips(TripsParams(vehicle_id, limit, offset, start, end))  (GET /trips)  → tripsState
  (web useSelectedVehicle)      → SelectedVehicleStore.selectedId → the optional vehicle_id filter
  (web useUnits/useFormatting)  → SettingsStore.settings()        → displayPrefs

NOTE — unlike the sibling DrivesList, the web trips query is NOT gated on a selected vehicle: it reads
  /trips with an OPTIONAL vehicle_id (web `vehicle_id: vehicleId ?? undefined`), so the ViewModel queries
  regardless and an absent/zero selection simply drops the filter (tripsQuery omits the key). The default
  365-day [today-365d, today] range + the page cursor (limit/offset) reproduce the web hook params.

SCOPE NOTE — the web page's PageContainer `actions` cluster (VehicleSelect, RangePicker, DataFreshnessAuto,
  SavedViewMenu) and the PullToRefresh wrapper are separate component parity units, not part of this page's
  manifest record (page:trips/TripList enumerates exactly the 7 panels + 2 charts + 3 states + 22 strings,
  requiredCount 34). They are intentionally not stubbed here (ADR-011: no placeholders, no scope drift). The
  query-freshness chip is still surfaced (header DataFreshness) and refresh()/retry() back the error surface.

SI BOUNDARY (P1/S5)
  The model stays SI end to end (meters, Wh, the raw RFC3339 date strings). Display conversion happens only at
  the render boundary via TripListDisplayPrefs (convertDistanceFromSI + the shared formatEnergy + the
  Wh/km→Wh/mi efficiency factor the web keeps because the shared units module ships no energy-per-distance
  helper) and the ChartFormat-backed number/currency formatters. The CSV/JSON share export emits the SI columns
  verbatim (distance_m, energy_wh). The cache stays SI (ADR-013); no non-SI value is stored or computed.

