STRING CATALOG
  21 of the 22 keys already existed in res/values/strings.xml (translation_trips_*, generated from the shared
  i18n catalog with the verbatim web inline-default values). One key — translation_trips_chart_title_aria — was
  absent from the web i18n source (the web only carries it as an inline `t(..., 'Top trips ranked by distance
  horizontal bar chart')` default), so it was added to res/values/strings.xml (an allowed file; sorted after
  translation_trips_chart_title) with the verbatim web default value. The default `values/` catalog is the only
  string source touched: the build runs no i18n generation, and MissingTranslation/ExtraTranslation are disabled
  (app/build.gradle.kts L114) because ar/he ship as full English fallback, so the ar/he mirrors are not required.
  Unit symbols ("km"/"mi", "Wh/mi"/"Wh/km", currency symbol), the "Trip #id" / "Trip id" name fallbacks, and the
  "In progress" duration label are reproduced verbatim from the web source, which likewise does not
  internationalize them (no i18n key exists for them on the web or in the required string set) — the same
  precedent the TripDetail port recorded.

A11Y / THEME / UNITS (ADR-015)
  - Each trailing TripRow metric carries a merged TalkBack content description ("<value> <caption>") via
    clearAndSetSemantics (TripRowMetric); the ChartContainer body carries the aria description
    (translation_trips_chart_title_aria) and exposes the accessible data table fallback for the opaque canvas.
  - Colours/typography come from MaterialTheme (P1/S9 tokens) — dark + dynamic colour honoured; the only fixed
    colours are the four per-card MetricCard accents (web `color="cyan|amber|green|purple"`), dynamic per-card
    values, not static theme tokens, matching the sibling DrivesList trend-palette precedent. Touch targets use
    the shared component sizing (Button/IconButton ≥48dp).
  - The stat grid is responsive: 2 columns on a phone, 4 on a ≥840dp window (web grid-cols-2 / lg:grid-cols-4).
  - SI values are converted only at the display boundary (TripListDisplayPrefs); the page is Compose-native —
    the bar chart uses the A3 Vico BarChartWrapper (no webview). The web page has no map (0 maps).

EXPORT (web exportAsCSV / exportAsJSON)
  The chart action's CSV + JSON buttons are wired to a real share handler (rememberTripExport): it serialises the
  loaded trips (CSV: the web id/name/start_date/end_date/distance_m/energy_wh/cost/drives/charges columns; JSON:
  the full SI Trip records via kotlinx.serialization) and opens the system share sheet via Intent.ACTION_SEND —
  the native analogue of the web browser download, no FileProvider/manifest wiring needed (the sibling
  TelemetryErrorsPanel precedent). Not a stub (ADR-011).

